693 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1832 0 R
/E (Which regions do you operate in, and which communities do you mainly support?)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
694 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 216 0 R
/E (Ans: We primarily focus on working with Scheduled Tribes \(ST\) and Scheduled Castes \(SC\), supporting several tribes and castes across these communities. Our primary region of operation is Madhya Pradesh, but we also extend our efforts into Chhattisgarh. Currently, however, many of our projects, including those funded by the Central Government, have been temporarily paused.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
695 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 216 0 R
/E (2. What do you think are the major challenges especially with regard to tribal communities in Madhya Pradesh? )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
696 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 216 0 R
/E (Ans: The main challenge is economic instability. Tribal communities rely on traditional practices and struggle to maintain their land and livelihoods. Government policies often hinder their growth, making it difficult for them to achieve financial stability and progress.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
697 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 216 0 R
/E (3. How is your NGO addressing these challenges? )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
698 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 216 0 R
/E (Ans: We address these issues through income support programs, awareness initiatives, and by preserving tribal culture and religion. We engage directly with the communities, as we share a similar cultural background, which helps build trust. While some external religious movements have tried, they haven't been as successful, particularly in Madhya Pradesh.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
699 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 216 0 R
/E (4. Where do your financial resources come from?)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
700 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 216 0 R
/E (Ans: Our financial resources primarily come from the Central Government's Tribal Ministry and the Social Welfare Ministry. We also receive contributions from the communities we work with. Additionally, we are seeking CSR funding for community health initiatives. We apply for and work on various projects as they become available, including funding from the Tribal Ministry and HID.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
